  "notes": "6 April 2024 — Maths only. BROKEN-numbering paper: source key untrustworthy, every answer BLIND-derived by an independent solver (compilation playbook). Shipped MCQ-letter + integer-NAT; dropped ambiguous.",
  "authoredSolutions": {
    "61": "\\(f'(x)=3x^2\\sin(1/x)-x\\cos(1/x)\\) for \\(x\\neq0\\). Then \\(f''(x)=6x\\sin(1/x)-4\\cos(1/x)-\\tfrac1x\\sin(1/x)\\). At \\(x=2/\\pi\\), \\(1/x=\\pi/2\\): \\(f''(2/\\pi)=\\tfrac{12}{\\pi}-\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}=\\tfrac{24-\\pi^2}{2\\pi}\\).",
    "62": "\\(\\vec{AB}=(-\\tfrac43,\\tfrac43,\\tfrac43),\\ \\vec{AC}=(-1,1,2),\\ \\vec{AD}=(\\tfrac13,-\\tfrac13,\\tfrac23)\\). \\(\\vec{AB}\\times\\vec{AC}=(\\tfrac43,\\tfrac43,0)\\Rightarrow\\) area\\(=2\\sqrt2/3\\); \\(\\vec{AC}\\times\\vec{AD}=(\\tfrac43,\\tfrac43,0)\\Rightarrow2\\sqrt2/3\\). Total \\(=4\\sqrt2/3\\).",
    "63": "\\(\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\frac{\\cos^2x\\sin^2x}{(\\cos^3x+\\sin^3x)^2}dx=\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\frac{\\tan^2x\\sec^2x}{(1+\\tan^3x)^2}dx\\). Let \\(u=\\tan^3x,\\ du=3\\tan^2x\\sec^2x\\,dx\\): \\(\\tfrac13\\int_0^1\\frac{du}{(1+u)^2}=\\tfrac13\\cdot\\tfrac12=\\tfrac16\\).",
    "64": "\\(\\sum x=200,\\ \\sum x^2=20(4+100)=2080\\). Corrected: \\(\\sum x=204,\\ \\bar x=10.2,\\ \\sum x^2=2080-64+144=2160\\). Var\\(=2160/20-10.2^2=108-104.04=3.96\\), SD\\(=\\sqrt{3.96}\\).",
    "65": "\\(x^2-4x+9=(x-2)^2+5>0\\), domain \\(\\mathbb R\\). Setting \\(y=f(x)\\): \\((y-1)x^2-(4y+2)x+(9y+15)=0\\), real \\(x\\Rightarrow5y^2+2y-16\\le0\\Rightarrow y\\in[-2,1.6]\\). Range bounded, non-monotonic: neither one-one nor onto.",
    "66": "Total integers in \\([100,700]=601\\). Multiples of 3: 200; of 4: 151; of 12: 50. Multiples of 3 or 4 \\(=200+151-50=301\\). Neither \\(=601-301=300\\).",
    "67": "By symmetry centre \\((0,k)\\), and distance to \\(y=\\sqrt3|x|\\) is \\(k/2=r\\). Touching parabola \\(y=6-x^2\\) at its vertex \\((0,6)\\): \\(k+r=6\\Rightarrow k=4,r=2\\). Circle \\(x^2+(y-4)^2=4\\); point \\((2,4)\\) satisfies it.",
    "68": "\\(C_1=r\\,C_2+(0,0,-2)^T\\), so the \\(r\\,C_2\\) part vanishes and \\(A_r\\) is independent of \\(r\\): expanding, \\(A_r=-2(n^2-\\beta)+4(\\tfrac{n^2}{2}+\\alpha)=4\\alpha+2\\beta\\). Hence \\(2A_{10}-A_8=4\\alpha+2\\beta\\).",
    "69": "\\(d_1=(2,-7,5),d_2=(2,1,-3),\\ d_1\\times d_2=(16,16,16),\\ |d_1\\times d_2|=16\\sqrt3\\). \\(P_2-P_1=(-4,16,0)\\), dot \\(=192\\). SD\\(=192/(16\\sqrt3)=12/\\sqrt3=4\\sqrt3\\).",
    "70": "\\(P(B\\mid S)=\\frac{0.4\\cdot0.9}{0.6\\cdot0.8+0.4\\cdot0.9}=\\frac{0.36}{0.84}=\\tfrac37\\). \\(126p=126\\cdot\\tfrac37=54\\).",
    "71": "With \\(s=t^2-5t+6,\\ \\alpha\\beta=1\\): \\(a_{n+1}=s\\,a_n-a_{n-1}\\), so \\(a_{2023}+a_{2025}=s\\,a_{2024}\\) and the ratio \\(=s\\). Minimum of \\(t^2-5t+6\\) is \\(-\\tfrac14\\) at \\(t=\\tfrac52\\).",
    "72": "\\(R_1:2x-3y=2\\Rightarrow(4,2),(7,4),(10,6),(13,8),(16,10),(19,12)\\): 6 pairs, add 6, \\(M=6\\). \\(R_2:5x=4y\\Rightarrow(4,5),(8,10),(12,15),(16,20)\\): 4 pairs, add 4, \\(N=4\\). \\(M+N=10\\).",
    "73": "Line through \\((4,-9)\\): \\(A=(4+9/m,0),\\ B=(0,-9-4m)\\). Sum \\(S=(4+9/m)+(9+4m)=13+9/m+4m\\). By AM-GM \\(9/m+4m\\ge12\\), so \\(S_{\\min}=25\\).",
    "74": "\\(f(x)=x^x=e^{x\\ln x}\\), \\(f'(x)=x^x(\\ln x+1)>0\\iff\\ln x>-1\\iff x\\ge1/e\\). Increasing on \\([1/e,\\infty)\\).",
    "75": "Inradius of equilateral triangle side 12: \\(r=12/(2\\sqrt3)=2\\sqrt3\\), so circle diameter \\(=4\\sqrt3\\). Inscribed square diagonal \\(=4\\sqrt3\\Rightarrow\\) side \\(=2\\sqrt6\\). Area \\(m=24\\), perimeter \\(n=8\\sqrt6\\), \\(n^2=384\\); \\(m+n^2=408\\).",
    "76": "Triangles from an \\(n\\)-gon with no side of the polygon \\(=\\tfrac{n(n-4)(n-5)}{6}\\). For \\(n=8\\): \\(\\tfrac{8\\cdot4\\cdot3}{6}=16\\).",
    "77": "\\(y'+\\tfrac{y}{1+x^2}=\\tfrac{e^{\\arctan x}}{1+x^2}\\), IF\\(=e^{\\arctan x}\\). Then \\(y\\,e^{\\arctan x}=\\tfrac12e^{2\\arctan x}+C\\), so \\(y=\\tfrac12e^{\\arctan x}+Ce^{-\\arctan x}\\). \\(y(1)=0\\Rightarrow C=-\\tfrac12e^{\\pi/2}\\); \\(y(0)=\\tfrac12-\\tfrac12e^{\\pi/2}=\\tfrac12(1-e^{\\pi/2})\\).",
    "78": "\\(y'+\\tfrac{y}{x\\ln x}=\\tfrac{3}{2x^2}\\), IF\\(=\\ln x\\). \\((y\\ln x)'=\\tfrac{3\\ln x}{2x^2}\\Rightarrow y\\ln x=-\\tfrac{3}{2x}(\\ln x+1)+C\\). \\(y(e^{-1})=0\\Rightarrow C=0\\). At \\(x=e\\): \\(y=-\\tfrac{3}{2e}(2)=-\\tfrac3e\\).",
    "79": "Vertices \\((0,0),(3,9),(9,0)\\). \\(A=\\int_0^3 x^{3/2}dx+\\int_3^9\\big[\\tfrac{27-3x}{2}-3x+x^{3/2}\\big]dx\\). The \\(x^{3/2}\\) parts give \\(\\tfrac25\\cdot243=97.2\\); polynomial part \\(\\int_3^9\\tfrac{27-9x}{2}dx=-81\\). \\(A=16.2\\), \\(10A=162\\).",
    "81": "Nontrivial solution needs \\(\\det\\begin{vmatrix}\\alpha&1&2\\\\1&\\beta&3\\\\2&2&\\gamma\\end{vmatrix}=0\\), i.e. \\(\\alpha\\beta\\gamma-6\\alpha-4\\beta-\\gamma+10=0\\). So \\(6\\alpha+4\\beta+\\gamma=\\alpha\\beta\\gamma+10=45+10=55\\).",
    "82": "\\(\\tfrac{dy}{dx}=\\tfrac{y+5}{2(x-3)}\\Rightarrow(y+5)^2=C(x-3)\\); through \\((4,-2)\\): \\(C=9\\), so \\((y+5)^2=9(x-3)\\), \\(a=9/4\\), directrix \\(x=3/4\\). Focal distance of \\((7,1)\\): \\(d=7-\\tfrac34=\\tfrac{25}{4}\\); \\(12d=75\\).",
    "83": "By parts, \\(I_{k+1}=7(k+1)(I_k-I_{k+1})\\Rightarrow r_k=\\tfrac{I_k}{I_{k+1}}=\\tfrac{7k+8}{7k+7}\\), so \\(r_k-1=\\tfrac{1}{7(k+1)}\\) and \\(\\tfrac{1}{7(r_k-1)}=k+1\\). \\(\\sum_{k=1}^{10}(k+1)=\\sum_{2}^{11}=65\\).",
    "84": "\\(P(x)=4\\prod(x-x_i)\\). \\(\\prod(4+x_i^2)=\\prod(x_i-2i)(x_i+2i)=\\tfrac{P(2i)P(-2i)}{16}\\). \\(P(2i)=141-88i\\), \\(P(-2i)=141+88i\\), product \\(=141^2+88^2=27625\\). \\(\\tfrac{27625}{16}=\\tfrac{125m}{16}\\Rightarrow m=221\\).",
    "85": "Tangents from \\((0,1)\\) to the parabola give slopes \\(0\\) and \\(-4/3\\) (\\(L_1,L_2\\)). Unit dirs \\((1,0),(3,-4)/5\\); bisectors \\((2,-1)\\) (slope \\(-1/2\\)) and \\((1,2)\\) (slope \\(2\\)). Base \\(QR\\perp\\) bisector \\(\\Rightarrow m_1=2,\\ m_2=-1/2\\). \\(16(4+\\tfrac14)=68\\).",
    "86": "\\(T_3/T_2=\\tfrac{n-1}{2}\\tfrac yx=\\tfrac29,\\ T_4/T_3=\\tfrac{n-2}{3}\\tfrac yx=\\tfrac19\\Rightarrow n=5,\\ y/x=1/9\\). \\(5x^4y=135,\\ x^4y=27\\) with \\(y=x/9\\Rightarrow x=3,y=1/3\\). \\(6(125+9+\\tfrac13)=806\\).",
    "87": "Solving \\(T_r=3T_{r-1}+6^r,\\ T_1=6\\): \\(T_r=2(6^r-3^r)\\). \\(S_n=\\tfrac35(4\\cdot6^n-5\\cdot3^n+1)\\). Matching \\(\\tfrac15(n^2-12n+39)(\\cdots)\\Rightarrow n^2-12n+39=3\\Rightarrow(n-6)^2=0\\Rightarrow n=6\\).",
    "88": "\\(\\cot^{-1}x=\\tan^{-1}(1/x)\\). \\(\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac13+\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac14=\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac{7}{11}\\), \\(+\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac15=\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac{23}{24}\\). Then \\(\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac1n=\\tfrac\\pi4-\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac{23}{24}=\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac1{47}\\Rightarrow n=47\\).",
    "89": "Line: \\((2-2t,-5+3t,11-4t)\\), dir \\((-2,3,-4)\\). Foot from \\(R(1,7,6)\\): \\(29t-58=0\\Rightarrow t=2\\), \\(Q=(-2,1,3)\\). \\(\\vec{PQ}=(-12,3,4)\\), \\(|PQ|=\\sqrt{144+9+16}=13\\).",
    "90": "\\(a\\times b+a\\times c+b\\times c=(1,8,13)\\); \\(a\\times b=(-1,22,17)\\Rightarrow(a+b)\\times c=(2,-14,-4)\\). With \\(a+b=(5,1,-1)\\) and \\(a\\cdot c=13\\): \\(c=(-1,-1,3)\\). \\(b\\cdot c=-22\\), so \\(24-b\\cdot c=46\\).",
    "151": "\\(Side halves each step. Perimeters: 3a,\\tfrac{3a}{2},\\ldots\\Rightarrow P=\\frac{3a}{1-1/2}=6a.\\) \\(Areas ratio \\tfrac14: Q=\\frac{(\\sqrt3/4)a^2}{1-1/4}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}a^2.\\) \\(Then P^2=36a^2=36\\sqrt3\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}a^2=36\\sqrt3\\,Q.\\)",
    "152": "\\(4x\\le 5y: x=1\\to5,\\,x=2\\to4,\\,x=3\\to3,\\,x=4\\to2,\\,x=5\\to2\\) pairs, so \\(m=16.\\) Reverses already present only for diagonal and \\((4,5),(5,4)\\); the \\(9\\) off-diagonal pairs lack reverses, so \\(n=9.\\) \\(m+n=25.\\)",
    "153": "\\(Total=5^3=125.\\) Exactly two addresses: \\(\\binom{5}{2}(2^3-2)=10\\cdot6=60.\\) \\(P=\\frac{60}{125}=\\frac{12}{25}.\\)",
    "154": "\\(M\\,dx+N\\,dy=0\\) is exact. Potential \\(F=\\frac{2+\\alpha}{2}x^2-\\beta xy+2x+\\alpha y^2+(\\beta\\gamma-4\\alpha)y.\\) Circle needs no \\(xy\\Rightarrow\\beta=0\\) and equal square coeffs \\(\\frac{2+\\alpha}{2}=\\alpha\\Rightarrow\\alpha=2.\\) Then \\(x^2+y^2+x-4y=0\\) (through origin), radius \\(=\\sqrt{\\tfrac14+4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.\\)",
    "155": "\\(16[(x-2)^2+(y-1)^2]=25[(x-1)^2+(y-3)^2]\\Rightarrow 9x^2+9y^2+14x-118y+170=0.\\) So \\(a=9,b=9,c=0,d=14,e=-118.\\) \\(a^2+2b+3c+4d+e=81+18+0+56-118=37.\\)",
    "156": "\\(Numerator\\sim n\\sum k^2-\\sum k^3\\sim \\frac{n^4}{3}-\\frac{n^4}{4}=\\frac{n^4}{12}.\\) Denominator \\(=(\\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2})^2-\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}\\sim\\frac{n^4}{4}.\\) Limit \\(=\\frac{1/12}{1/4}=\\frac13.\\)",
    "157": "\\(\\frac{^{n+1}C_{r+1}}{^{n}C_r}=\\frac{n+1}{r+1}=\\frac{11}{7}\\Rightarrow 7n-11r=4.\\) \\(\\frac{^{n}C_r}{^{n-1}C_{r-1}}=\\frac{n}{r}=\\frac{5}{3}\\Rightarrow n=\\frac{5r}{3}.\\) Solving: \\(r=6,n=10.\\) \\(2n+5r=20+30=50.\\)",
    "158": "\\(Work=17m.\\) With crashes day \\(k\\) has \\(m-4(k-1)\\) systems over \\(25\\) days: \\(\\sum_{k=1}^{25}(m-4(k-1))=25m-4\\cdot300=25m-1200.\\) Set \\(=17m\\Rightarrow8m=1200\\Rightarrow m=150.\\)",
    "159": "\\(|z_1-2z_2|=|1-2z_1\\bar z_2|.\\) Squaring: \\(|z_1|^2+4|z_2|^2=1+4|z_1|^2|z_2|^2\\Rightarrow(1-4|z_2|^2)(|z_1|^2-1)=0.\\) So \\(|z_1|=1\\) or \\(|z_2|=\\tfrac12.\\)",
    "160": "\\(g(x)=x^{1/x}\\) is maximised at \\(x=e\\), so \\(e^{1/e}>\\pi^{1/\\pi}.\\) Raising to \\(e\\pi\\): \\(e^{\\pi}>\\pi^{e}.\\)",
    "161": "\\(|c-a|^2=|c|^2-12|c|+38=8\\Rightarrow|c|=6+\\sqrt6\\) (since \\(|c|\\ge6\\)). \\(a\\times b=\\hat i-\\hat j+5\\hat k,\\;|a\\times b|=3\\sqrt3.\\) \\(|(a\\times b)\\times c|=3\\sqrt3(6+\\sqrt6)\\sin60^\\circ=\\frac{9}{2}(6+\\sqrt6).\\)",
    "162": "\\(Letters A,G,N,P,R,U.\\) Blocks of \\(120\\): A,G to \\(240\\), so \\(315th\\) is \\(75th\\) of N. NR block (\\(49\\)-\\(72\\)... ) leads to NRA, then NRAP, giving NRAPGU.",
    "163": "\\(g'(x)=h'(e^x)e^x e^{h(x)}+h(e^x)e^{h(x)}h'(x).\\) At \\(x=0\\) (with \\(h(0)=0,h(1)=1,h'(0)=h'(1)=2\\)): \\(g'(0)=h'(1)+h(1)h'(0)=2+1\\cdot2=4.\\)",
    "164": "\\(Foot of \\perp from Q(3,-3,1) on line: t=-1,F=(-1,2,2).\\) Image \\(P=2F-Q=(-5,7,3).\\) \\(PQ\\times PR=(36,18,54),\\;\\lambda^2=\\frac14(36^2+18^2+54^2)=1134.\\) \\(K=1134/14=81.\\)",
    "165": "\\(AP\\perp BC:\\;h+3k=17.\\) \\(BP\\perp AC:\\;h+k=3.\\) Solving \\(C=(-4,7).\\) \\(h^2+k^2=16+49=65\\Rightarrow x^2+y^2-65=0.\\)",
    "166": "\\(\\sin5x\\in[-1,1]\\Rightarrow7-\\sin5x\\in[6,8]\\Rightarrow f\\in[\\tfrac18,\\tfrac16].\\)",
    "167": "\\(a\\times(\\hat i+\\hat j)=(1,-1,1);\\;\\times\\hat i=(0,1,1);\\;\\times\\hat i=(0,1,-1)=b.\\) \\(a\\cdot b=2,|b|=\\sqrt2,\\) projection \\(=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt2}=\\sqrt2,\\) square \\(=2.\\)",
    "168": "\\(Area=\\int_1^2\\left(\\frac1x-\\frac{a}{x^2}\\right)dx=[\\ln x+\\tfrac{a}{x}]_1^2=\\ln2-\\tfrac{a}{2}.\\) Set \\(=\\ln2-\\tfrac17\\Rightarrow a=\\tfrac27.\\) \\(7a-3=2-3=-1.\\)",
    "169": "\\(\\int\\frac{dx}{a^2\\sin^2x+b^2\\cos^2x}=\\frac1{ab}\\tan^{-1}(\\tfrac{a}{b}\\tan x).\\) So \\(\\tfrac1{ab}=\\tfrac1{12},\\tfrac{a}{b}=3\\Rightarrow a=6,b=2.\\) Max of \\(a\\sin x+b\\cos x=\\sqrt{36+4}=\\sqrt{40}.\\)",
    "170": "\\(Order 3: \\det(\\mathrm{adj}\\,M)=\\det(M)^2,\\;\\det(kM)=k^3\\det M.\\) Tracking from \\((2A)^{-1}\\) with \\(\\det A=3\\): final \\(\\det=2^{-36}3^{20}.\\) \\(m=-36,n=20,\\;m+2n=4.\\)",
    "171": "\\([\\tfrac{x}{2}+3]\\) jumps at \\(x=2,4,6,8;\\;[\\sqrt x]\\) jumps at \\(x=1,4.\\) At \\(x=4\\) both jump \\(+1\\Rightarrow f\\) continuous. Discontinuities: \\(\\{1,2,6,8\\},\\) sum \\(=17.\\)",
    "173": "\\(S(x)=\\sum_{k=1}^{60}k t^k,\\,t=1+x.\\) \\(60^2S(60)=3600S(60)=61(1+59\\cdot61^{61})=3599\\cdot61^{61}+61.\\) So \\(a=3599,b=61,\\;a+b=3660.\\)",
    "174": "\\(\\int_0^3[x^2]dx=21-3\\sqrt2-\\sqrt3-\\sqrt5-\\sqrt6-\\sqrt7.\\) \\(\\int_0^3[\\tfrac{x^2}{2}]dx=10-3\\sqrt2-\\sqrt6.\\) Sum \\(=31-6\\sqrt2-\\sqrt3-\\sqrt5-2\\sqrt6-\\sqrt7.\\) So \\(a=31,b=-6,c=-2,\\;a+b+c=23.\\)",
    "175": "\\(Hypergeometric N=12,K=3,n=5:\\;\\mathrm{Var}=5\\cdot\\tfrac{3}{12}\\cdot\\tfrac{9}{12}\\cdot\\tfrac{7}{11}=\\frac{105}{176}.\\) \\(m=105,n=176,\\;n-m=71.\\)",
    "176": "\\(\\cos A=\\frac{15+c^2}{16c}=\\frac23\\Rightarrow3c^2-32c+45=0\\Rightarrow c=9.\\) \\(\\cos C=\\frac{49+64-81}{112}=\\frac27.\\) \\(\\cos3C=4(\\tfrac27)^3-3\\cdot\\tfrac27=-\\frac{262}{343}.\\) \\(49\\cos3C+42=-\\tfrac{262}{7}+42=\\frac{32}{7}.\\) \\(m+n=39.\\)",
    "177": "\\(d_1\\times d_2=(-6,-15,3),|d_1\\times d_2|=3\\sqrt{30}.\\) \\((P_2-P_1)\\cdot(d_1\\times d_2)=6\\lambda+126.\\) \\(\\frac{|6\\lambda+126|}{3\\sqrt{30}}=\\frac{44}{\\sqrt{30}}\\Rightarrow|6\\lambda+126|=132\\Rightarrow\\lambda=1\\) or \\(-43.\\) Largest \\(|\\lambda|=43.\\)",
    "178": "\\(Recurrence: U_n=-\\sqrt{2}\\,U_{n-1}+8U_{n-2}\\Rightarrow U_{10}+\\sqrt{2}\\,U_9=8U_8.\\) Hence \\(\\frac{U_{10}+\\sqrt{2}\\,U_9}{2U_8}=\\frac{8U_8}{2U_8}=4.\\)",
    "179": "\\(Solve first two for x,y in z, substitute into third; identity requires constant: 22+\\mu=-17\\Rightarrow\\mu=-39,\\) and \\(z\\)-coeff: \\(119\\lambda+119=0\\Rightarrow\\lambda=-1.\\) \\(\\lambda-\\mu=-1+39=38.\\)",
    "180": "\\(\\cot x\\,dx=-\\frac{e^y}{e^y+1}dy\\Rightarrow\\sin x(e^y+1)=C.\\) At \\((\\tfrac{\\pi}{2},0):C=2.\\) At \\(x=\\tfrac{\\pi}{6}:\\tfrac12(e^y+1)=2\\Rightarrow e^y=3.\\)"
  }
}
